WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.668
New evidence of hope

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.036
that four children

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.205
may be alive after a small plane

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.140
crash 17 days ago

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.108
in a remote part of the

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.175
Amazon rainforest.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.577
Here's why there is reason to hope.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.412
Discoveries of scrunchies,

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.447
plastic wrappings, even a baby bottle.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:15.648
CNN's

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.584
Stephanie Postman is in Colombia,

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.486
where this massive search

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.354
is currently underway.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.791
To discover a glimmer of hope.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.092
Colombia's president

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.861
tweeting that four children on board

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.262
a single engine aircraft

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.631
that crashed in the jungle on May 1st

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.601
had been found alive and well.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.436
Rescuers using scatter debris

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.470
to trace them.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.505
But on Thursday,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.607
the president's tweet was deleted,

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.841
saying the information

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.643
quote, could not be confirmed.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.844
Government officials blaming

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.113
poor communication.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.915
And the head of the country's

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.884
children welfare authority later

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.419
saying she was, quote,

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.654
very confident about their rescue.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.056
She said, quote,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.923
We're still missing

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.858
that very, very last link

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.560
that confirms all our hopes

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.162
until we have the food of the kids,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.596
we won't be stopping.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.998
We not underestimating

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.599
the information we received,

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.902
but we want to confirm directly ourselves

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:11.471
The Colombian

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.173
armed forces have been using dogs

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.641
to search for the children.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.009
The plane had taken off

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.311
from the remote area of Ararat, Kwara

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.846
bound for San Jose.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.015
We walk away.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.283
Rescuers from the military

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.217
and local indigenous

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.652
communities are in giving them

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.420
hope to bring home the little ones

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.422
as they follow a trail of small objects

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.825
such as hair scrunchies and baby bottles,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.261
or even bringing in a recording

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.062
of the grandmother

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.764
to at least one of the children

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.866
to help in the search

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.568
But efforts are difficult

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.002
given the rainfall in the dense

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.104
part of the jungle.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.738
Once the rivers start to swell

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.473
and things like that,

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.108
and you have areas that are rapids

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.243
that makes it more difficult to navigate.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.377
Obviously, as I said,

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.645
rivers are kind of the highway,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:53.179
so they're going to be

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.681
using those waterways

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.015
to get to and from places,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.884
obviously to extract

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.785
the survivors out

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.220
and things of that nature.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.921
The Colombian aviation authorities say

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.323
they found another three bodies

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.924
inside this small aircraft,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.893
but those have yet to be recovered.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.365
And, Jake,

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.166
CNN has just

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.267
learned minutes ago

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.068
that those bodies,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:15.768
the three bodies,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.103
have indeed been recovered

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.838
and have just arrived in the hands

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.740
of Colombian authorities.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.675
They were the bodies of the three adults

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.043
on board of that flight,

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.779
two indigenous passengers and the pilots.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.314
Still no words

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.682
on the whereabouts

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.117
and the status of those

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.485
four little children,

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.154
which makes these frantic search

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.688
even more frantic Jake.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.190
Stefan Campos, thank you so much.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:37.824
Appreciate it.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.025
Joining us now to discuss

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:39.259
and get

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.994
some insight is survival expert

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.263
and author Dave Canterbury.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.430
Dave, thank you so much for sharing

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.099
part of your afternoon with us.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:46.666
First,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.368
I just want to put the challenge

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.069
that these kids are facing

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.238
and the context you're talking about,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.775
some of the densest rainforest on Earth.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.943
What are they facing

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.113
Well, the

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:00.747
one thing I think

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:01.814
you have to put into context

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.017
is that these are indigenous people.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.752
They're they're tribal people,

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.320
children of tribal people.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.455
So they probably have some knowledge

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.523
of the local flora,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.658
fauna and things like that

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:12.959
and what they can use off the landscape.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.795
However, surviving the plane crash alone.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.797
That's phenomenal in itself.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:18.665
And then

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.133
the fact that they have the four year old

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.935
or the 11 month old child

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.570
becomes the anomaly

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.470
because that child

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.272
probably needs much more care

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.407
than the older children do.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.141
And the older children

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.510
are probably leading this expedition out.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:31.911
Would they be better off

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.213
staying in place to be found?

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.281
I would say yes, obviously they would.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:35.848
However, they're

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.649
probably thinking

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.618
that if they keep moving toward water,

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.520
water becomes the highway in a jungle.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.488
So the closer they can get the water,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.490
the closer they are to being found.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.892
That's a really important point.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:46.593
It's interesting

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.493
you described

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.162
the baby as being the anomaly

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.296
maybe for survivalist.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:50.863
It's the anomaly,

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:51.931
but the whole situation

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.933
seems like something out of fiction.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.167
Right.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:54.867
And apparently

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.237
the weather isn't helping either.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.271
There's a lot of rain

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.572
falling in that area.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.274
How does that complicate this process?

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:03.876
Once the

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.510
river start

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.678
to swell and things like that

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.347
and you have areas that are rapids

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.449
that makes it more difficult to navigate.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.550
Obviously, as I said,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.851
the rivers are kind of the highway.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.652
So they're going to be using

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.920
those waterways

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.688
to get to and from places, obviously,

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.991
to extract the survivors out

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.125
and things of that nature.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.560
And that is more difficult

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.894
during torrential rains

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.997
when those rivers are swollen

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.031
and they've been out there

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.899
for more than two weeks now.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.501
If you're, you know,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.502
a child,

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.803
you're in a plane crash,

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.405
something horrible like that happens.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.940
You see loved ones

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.342
that might be injured or killed.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:37.910
What's your first step?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.612
I mean, what do you do in that situation

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.680
if you're in the middle of the Amazon

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.350
Well, being a child, it's

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:44.584
hard to

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.152
say what their thought process

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.554
would be from a survival standpoint.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.023
Obviously, to

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.824
understand what injuries they may have

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:52.992
from the plane crash itself

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.394
and attend to those injuries first.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.629
And then once that's taken care of,

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.031
it becomes a simple system

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.732
of sheltering ourselves

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.200
from any extra elements,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.402
making sure that we have water.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.303
And in torrential rains,

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.937
they're going to have plenty of water

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.372
and then sustainable food,

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.807
especially for the younger ones

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.642
who require food more often.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.311
And then are they going to navigate

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.945
toward a waterway, like I said,

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:13.946
or try to stay put?

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.214
I tend to believe that

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.417
because these tribal children

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.352
are probably from a river

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.120
oriented tribe to begin with,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.121
they probably understand

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.389
that moving toward water

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.458
is their best bet for rescue,

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.793
going from one body of water

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.127
to a larger body of water

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.629
to a larger body of water.

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:30.630
They here at the largest river,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.732
they can find to find something

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.167
in the form of civilization

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.769
or someone traveling to and from.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.004
That's really important context.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:39.772
These are indigenous children.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.307
They're part of a local tribe.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.443
So they probably have some awareness

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.211
of the rainforest and the fauna

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.846
and what to eat and what not.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.748
But it's still kind of scary

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.215
being out there

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.351
with so many things, being poisonous

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.285
and venomous. Right.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.188
Oh, there's no question.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.856
I mean, you've got large

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:57.323
predators

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:57.623
out there

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.358
like Jaguar,

00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.225
you've got poisonous

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:01.094
snakes, you've got venomous spiders.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.362
All those types of things are out there,

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:02.862
not to mention

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.263
just the constant

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.065
pestering of insects in general

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.900
and then the constant rain, which is

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.136
what would be a large morale factor

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.671
for someone like us,

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.806
but someone who lives in that day

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.807
in and day out.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.543
Probably not as much of a downfall

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.010
and morale

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.545
as it would be for someone like us.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.180
But I think that just the fact

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:21.781
that these children,

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.216
as young as they are,

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.517
realizing a 13 year

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.284
old child

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.486
growing up in that environment

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.720
probably is going to be very similar

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.588
to someone

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:29.222
growing up around

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:29.989
the eastern woodlands

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:31.090
of the United States are going to know

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.258
what to stay away from,

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:33.693
what they can eat, what they can eat,

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.794
things like that.

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.596
However, alone

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:37.797
without any one around

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.632
definitely is going to be a challenge.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:40.767
And especially with that

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:43.035
11 month old baby. Yikes.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:43.803
That is tough,

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:46.005
but it sounds like they're at least alive

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.974
and hopefully they'll be found soon.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:48.741
Dave Canterbury,

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:49.409
thank you so much

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.043
for sharing your perspective with us.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:51.644
We'd love to chat

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:52.678
more once they are found.

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:55.381
Absolutely, sir.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:55.748
Thank you.

